  "evidence": "TEXT_E: Recruit 20,000 nurses and 10,000 doctors; faster treatment free at the point of use; recruit 10,000 teachers and raise secondary standards; retain winter fuel payment and raise the minimum wage to £4.20; add 6,000 police and reform the criminal justice system; restructure benefits to support into work; enhance support for children and pensioners; strong, accountable local government. TEXT_C: Increase NHS funding and nurse pay; simplify benefits to ensure work always pays and reduce fraud; raise income tax threshold to remove ~1 million low earners from tax; increase police by 25,000 with community-linked policing and ‘life means life’ for the most serious crimes; leave the EU and enact a UK Bill of Rights preventing sovereignty transfer; selection/streaming, vouchers, and specialist/faith school options.",
  "reasoning": "Given the profile’s strongest weights on Care and Authority, followed by Equality, TEXT_E centers on expanding NHS and schools, supporting pensioners and families, and boosting police while reforming justice—directly appealing to care, authority, and equality. TEXT_C strongly reflects authority and proportionality (sovereignty, tougher justice, work-pay linkage) but places more emphasis on loyalty and market-based education/selection that undercut equality, which is a higher priority in the profile than loyalty.",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "winner": "TEXT_E"
}
